problems.problem:
A set of $n$ lamps, numbered from $1$ to $n$, are initially off. At each moment, it is possible to perform one of the following operations:

• change the state of lamp $1$;
• change the state of lamp $2$, provided lamp $1$ is on;
• change the state of lamp $k > 2$, provided lamp $k-1$ is on and all the lamps $1, \dots, k-2$ are off.

Show that it is possible, after a certain number of operations, to have only lamp $n$ on.
